  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "An array BBB of size 2⋅M2 \\cdot M2⋅M is called good if the following condition holds:\n\n\nFor each i=1,2,…,Mi = 1, 2, \\ldots, Mi=1,2,…,M, B2⋅i−1=B2⋅iB_{2 \\cdot i - 1} = B_{2 \\cdot i}B2⋅i−1​=B2⋅i​.\nFor example, B=[1,1,3,3]B = [1, 1, 3, 3]B=[1,1,3,3] and B=[4,4]B = [4, 4]B=[4,4] are good, but B=[1,1,2]B = [1, 1, 2]B=[1,1,2] is not.\n\nYou are given an array AAA of length NNN. Find the length of longest subsequence of AAA which is good.\n\nA subsequence is formed by deleting several elements from the array without changing the order of the remaining elements. Notably, a subsequence does not need to be contiguous.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains NNN - the size of the array.\nThe second line contains A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, - the elements of the array.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the length of the longest good subsequence of AAA.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤N1 \\le A_i \\le N1≤Ai​≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
